    description: "When no config.yaml.template exists, setup falls back to built-in defaults silently. For teams that want to customize governance (field schemas, status transitions, sync thresholds), a version-controlled template is useful. Suggest opt-in: 'htrac setup --write-template' writes built-in defaults as .agent/tracker/config.yaml.template. Not automatic since most single-user repos don't need it. Weakest of the four setup gaps but still reasonable for multi-contributor projects. Source: independent analyst review (tracker_feedback_03172026.txt)."  # 2c86
